{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/849348-wondered-a-while-how-are-banality-and-glamour-more-then-opposites","id":849348,"title":"Wondered a while how are Banality and Glamour more then opposites?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-18T10:55:09-07:00","id":849348,"title":"Wondered a while how are Banality and Glamour more then opposites?","content":"how Are the two traits more then opposite of each other?<br /> <br /> Whats it mean to have a Banality of 7 and Glamour of 8.<br /> <br /> I KNOW what it means mechanicly, mind you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 03-18-2016, 01:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T11:19:15-07:00","id":849356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/849348-wondered-a-while-how-are-banality-and-glamour-more-then-opposites#post849348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">how Are the two traits more then opposite of each other?<br /> <br /> Whats it mean to have a Banality of 7 and Glamour of 8.<br /> <br /> I KNOW what it means mechanicly, mind you.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It means you are creative and mused so many people, but you are about to lose in your mundane life, and do not have any time to spare on dreaming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7562-kokorowatari","name":"KokoroWatari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T08:42:30-07:00","id":850137,"title":"","content":"It's possible, although rare, to have both high Glamour and high Banality. I tend to think of Glamour as something inherent and Banality as something external that settles on you. Like the Dust in His Dark Materials.<br /> <br /> High Glamour means you're creative, and your spirit is still connected to the Dreaming in some fashion. But high Banality means that your mortal flesh is starting to weigh down on your faerie soul. The dust of Banality has accumulated over time and, even though you have high Glamour and theoretically do have the capacity to shed some of it, you've not managed to navigate the middle path in such a way as to prevent this from oppressing your faerie nature.<br /> <br /> A character that retains high Glamour should, in theory, have a good chance to lower their Banality through quests and the like, but Banality catches up with everyone in the end and not everyone is adept at looking after their own wellbeing, even if they are magically aware beings with half-faerie souls and buckets of creativity and imagination.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T22:49:07-07:00","id":853347,"title":"","content":"Banality isn't necessarily a bad thing. It might wear away at one's faerie soul, but it also roots one in the mundane world. Banality is what reminds you to pay your bills and mail the rent check and buy groceries, otherwise known as &quot;the stuff that keeps you sheltered and warm and fed&quot;. It's when the amounts get too extreme, or there's too much gap between them, that problems crop up. Too little Banality with too much Glamour, and you're living in a perpetual Hangover universe. Too much Banality with too little Glamour, and you're basically in Office Space.<br /> <br /> For a general example: I had a satyr once, years ago, with a Seelie Legacy of Pishogue. She was almost always two hairs and one strange day away from Bedlam. To counteract this a bit, she had a job flipping burgers, something boring and mundane and repetitive, to remind herself that she couldn't just follow the multicolor hallucinated butterflies and dance off into fairyland, because it's Not A Good Thing when one is human and mortal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T02:03:22-07:00","id":853399,"title":"","content":"Many of the people I know in really, really banal jobs have incredibly 'on the edge' lifestyles. They veer from mind-numbing monotony to bacchanalian revelry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}